Stadium Analysis Page
Overview & Purpose
This section analyzes venue utilization, capacity limits, geographic distribution, and overall spectator attendance efficiency across hosted matches.

Key Insights
Scale & Reach: The tournament hosted 104 matches across 16 stadiums, attracting an aggregate total of 6.81 million spectators.

Attendance Benchmark: The average attendance per match reached 65,490 fans, with the peak stadium capacity topping out at 80,824.

Flagship Venues: MetLife Stadium (New York) and Estadio Azteca (Mexico City) achieved the highest overall capacity usage and attendance totals.

Regional Hubs: Host cities such as East Rutherford, Arlington, and Inglewood led in total fan turnout across scheduled fixtures.
